WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.140
A bug in

00:00:00.951 --> 00:00:02.979
Java's fastest Base64

00:00:02.791 --> 00:00:03.545
decoder

00:00:04.086 --> 00:00:05.619
An OpenJDK pull

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.185
request

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.272
number 32781

00:00:08.485 --> 00:00:11.951
fixes issue 8392044

00:00:12.046 --> 00:00:14.545
the AVX-512 Base64

00:00:14.357 --> 00:00:15.748
decoder overwrites

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.751
its output buffer

00:00:16.562 --> 00:00:17.305
on a short

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.048
padded tail

00:00:18.574 --> 00:00:19.470
The bug sits

00:00:19.282 --> 00:00:21.474
in the x86-64

00:00:21.298 --> 00:00:23.574
AVX-512 VBMI path

00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:25.213
of generate base64

00:00:25.036 --> 00:00:26.062
decode block

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.441
the hand-tuned stub

00:00:27.253 --> 00:00:28.845
behind fast decoding

00:00:29.366 --> 00:00:30.557
Leftover tails of

00:00:30.368 --> 00:00:31.594
one to sixty-three

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:32.278
bytes use a

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.682
masked vector sequence

00:00:33.505 --> 00:00:34.460
that computes the

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:35.462
output size as

00:00:35.274 --> 00:00:36.429
length over four

00:00:36.347 --> 00:00:37.290
times three

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:38.844
Full story on

00:00:38.655 --> 00:00:39.551
the dashboard
